course: dictionary
lesson: 9181
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Soar is a good example. «Eagles soar above the valley» means they fly high in the air. «Prices soared» means prices rose very quickly. Same word, different picture.
explain: Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence. Is it about birds or the sky? Then flying is likely. Is it about money, numbers or temperatures? Then the meaning is going up fast. Check by swapping in your meaning: «prices flew» does not quite work, so soared here means rose quickly.
explain: Feelings can soar too. «Her heart soared» means she suddenly felt great joy, as if she were lifting off the ground. Spirits and hopes can soar in the same way.
fact: Soar means to fly high in the air, often gliding without flapping much.
fact: «Eagles soar» on rising warm air, and storks soar on rising warm air called thermals.
fact: Soar can also mean to rise very quickly, as in «temperatures soared to 40°C».
fact: Soar can mean to rise up tall, as in «mountains soaring above the valley».
fact: If your spirits or hopes soar, you suddenly feel very happy and hopeful.
exercise: «Vultures soar most in the hot middle of the day.» What does soar mean here? | To dig deep into the ground | To sink slowly into water | *To fly high in the air, gliding | To shout loudly
exercise: «Sales soared after the new advert.» What does soared mean here? | Flew away over the roofs | *Rose very quickly | Fell down slowly
exercise: «Her heart soared when she won the race.» What feeling does soared show? | Tiredness | Hunger | *Great joy | Sadness
test: «Mountains soaring above the valley looked huge.» What does soaring mean? | Hiding under the ground | Shrinking | *Rising up tall | Crumbling away
test: Jess wrote, «The price of bread soared.» Which meaning fits best? | Flew up like a bird | Went down slowly | *Rose quickly | Stopped completely
exam: Which sentence uses soar to mean rise very quickly? | *The temperature soared to 40 degrees | The storks soared on warm air | The eagle soared over the hills
